@startuml anthonys_face_first_enrollment
 title Anthony's Face Lab - face first, name confirmation, atomic enrollment
 skinparam shadowing false
 actor Operator
 participant "Enroll / camera" as UI
 participant "Discovery" as Match
 participant "Enrollment coordinator" as Flow
 participant "Configured liveness and capture" as Checks
 database "localStorage schema 5" as DB
 Operator -> UI : Start live scan
 UI -> Match : detections and probe embeddings keyed by detection ID
 Match -> Match : independent stability and >=0.85 matching for each track
 Match --> UI : each face has its own candidate, thumbnail, score and status
 alt confirmed existing enrollee
   Match --> UI : matched record; hold identity while track continues
   Operator -> UI : explicitly add / replace a sample
 else stable unknown tracked face
   Match --> UI : name field in Current match similarity
   Operator -> UI : name + Enter; acknowledge browser-local storage
 end
 UI -> Flow : nameDetectedFace(track ID, name or matched person ID)
 Flow -> Match : verify fresh same track and unchanged gallery
 Flow -> Flow : bind target; keep new person in memory
 Flow -> Checks : configured challenges and fresh same-pose consistency
 Checks --> Flow : ready; request capture automatically
 alt successful single enrollment
   Flow -> DB : saveEnrollment(newPerson?, template, attempt)
   DB -> DB : recheck identity, scope, capacity and evidence
   DB --> UI : one atomic write; resume discovery
 else optional guided set
   Flow --> UI : sealed three-sample review
   Operator -> UI : Save three samples
   Flow -> DB : addSampleSet(newPerson?, captures)
 else loss / ambiguity / cancellation
   Flow --> UI : discard bound draft; require name confirmation again
 end
 note over Flow, DB
   Multiple faces keep independent analysis and per-face capture sessions.
   At most two crops per comparison; rotate fairly across detections.
   No empty person row from typing a name.
   Failed writes preserve existing data and retry the same capture.
   No selection or diagnostic image mode on Enroll.
   Diagnostic images remain available in Settings.
 end note
@enduml


@startuml anthonys_parallel_enrollment
